# PilotFish interface construction

When creating, scaffolding, expanding, or design-documenting a PilotFish interface under `Clients/`:

0. **First action for a net-new demo:** shut down **all other** Sandbox demo Docker stacks under `Clients/` (`python3 tools/list_sandbox_demo_docker.py`, then `docker compose down` for each idle demo — no `-v` / prune unless the user asks). Then create `Clients/Demos/<Category>/…/<slug>/` (`python3 tools/scaffold_demo_stage.py --slug … --title … --port …`; category is inferred, or pass `--category Insurance/EDI` / `Medical/HL7` / `Medical/FHIR` / `Other`). That starts `docker compose --profile stage` by default. Announce localhost + LAN URLs immediately. Do not leave the user staring at an empty chat while scaffolding happens silently.
1. **Read and follow** `docs/INTERFACE_CONSTRUCTION_PLAYBOOK.md` end-to-end.
2. **Choose modules from** the external docs project at `/Users/brianhannan/Documents/PilotFish Documentation` (see `PilotFish_Documentation/DOCUMENTATION_LOCATION.txt`; use `Documents/` for tracker + deep dives) and `PilotFish_V2/` (`modules.conf` + `com/pilotfish/eip/modules` Java). EIP modules are shared with V1 — use that code to learn FQCNs and config items. Do not invent class names.
3. **Assemble runtime as V1** `pilotfish/demo-eip-root/**/route.xml` for `pilotfish-eip:23R1`. Copy a Sandbox demo skeleton when one exists for those classes. **Generate V2** (`route.v2.xml`) for Routes tab / PDF. `PilotFish_V2` is for module + format knowledge — not “author V2-only runtime” unless the user overrides.
4. **Do not invent** a one-off layout — after module selection, copy the closest demo (`edi-837-snip-sqlserver`, `hl7-healthcare-automation`, or `http-post-to-rabbitmq` for HTTP Post → RabbitMQ) and delete unused pieces. Tools find those by **slug** under `Clients/Demos/<Category>/…/<slug>/`. **Exception — public PilotFish page/video:** match that video’s Source/Target Transform **format** stages on the first build (`.cursor/rules/website-verbatim-demo.mdc`). Do **not** copy a Relay + Listener-processor shortcut (`csv-sftp-to-sql`). Reference: `hl7-interface-engine-demo`.
5. **Before coding:** capture pre-flight answers and create `DESIGN.md` from the playbook §8 template (include chosen FQCNs in the Pipeline table).
6. **No silent drift** between runtime V1 and diagram V2; call out doc/WAR version skew (e.g. 26R1 docs vs 23R1 image) in DESIGN.md.
7. **No compliance theater:** stages named Validate / SNIP / Split must gate, validate the wire artifact, or truly fork — otherwise rename and document.
8. **No hardcoded X12/HL7 wire text:** when generating EDI or HL7, XSLT builds PilotFish structured EDI XML / HL7 XML, then `EDITransformationProcessor` (`XML to EDI`) or `HL7TransformationProcessor` (`XML to HL7 2.X`). Never concatenate `ISA*…` or `MSH|…` as `xsl:output method="text"` for new work (playbook §3.5). `edi-278-prior-auth` is the demo reference.
9. **X12 TableData (required for EDI demos):** use repo-root `EDI/TableData/x12` (playbook §3.6 + `EDI/README.md`). Mount it to `eip-root/edi-tabledata`, set `UseInternalData=false` + `USE_ENHANCED_CONTEXT=true` + `TransactionDataWithVersion` → `edi-tabledata/<IG>` (`5010`). Prefer TableData `examples/*.edi` / XSDs when they improve the demo; keep story-specific `samples/` when logic depends on them.
10. **No claim-before-complete** and **no dual-write without compensation** unless explicitly listed as an accepted demo risk in `DESIGN.md`.
11. **Ship:** README (ports + smoke cmds), bounded polls/throttling for heavy stages, kickout/poison story, Web UI + route-viewer when routes are part of the deliverable (copy `diagram-groups.js` from `fhir-r4-platform`; prefer `config=compact` for committed route PDFs).
12. **Always generate the route design PDF** into `documents/`. For long processor chains (≥4 in a row or ≥8 on a worker), author `diagram-groups.json` and export **overview (collapsed groups) + later detail pages** per playbook §6.1b (`python3 tools/export_route_diagrams.py --config compact`). Do this for every new interface without waiting to be asked.
13. **LAN access (required on spin-up):** detect the host `192.*` address, keep Web UI published on `0.0.0.0` (not `127.0.0.1`-only), set compose `LAN_HINT=http://<192.x.x.x>:<webui-port>/`, and announce **both** localhost and LAN URLs in README + the agent summary whenever the UI is running. **Same URLs on the Info tab:** every link you paste in chat (Local Web UI, LAN, EIP, HTTP POST path, FTP/SFTP, SQL, RabbitMQ management, mock payer, … plus demo credentials) must also appear in the Info tab **Access** list (`info_urls` in Flask; playbook §6.5). Chat-only links are a miss.
14. **Browser links for every review PDF (required):** serve PDFs from the Web UI under `/documents/…` (mount `documents/`), verify HTTP 200 + `application/pdf` on the LAN IP, and paste **both** localhost and `http://192.x.x.x:<port>/documents/<file>.pdf` in the agent summary. Do not rely on Google Drive alone (credentials often expire); Drive upload is optional extra only.
15. **Done only after** smoke test (§7 of the playbook), grouped route PDF in `documents/` when §6.1b applies, LAN UI + PDF browser URLs configured/announced, and a plain-language list of limitations.
16. **Build timing (required):** on the user’s first ask to create a demo, record UTC `started_at` in `documents/build-timing.json` (schema: `docs/templates/build-timing.example.json`). Track phase start/end times (design, scaffold, routes, Web UI, PDFs/tests). When the user deems the demo complete, set `completed_at`, rank `slowest_phases`, note bottlenecks/speedup ideas, and summarize total minutes + top slow phases in chat (playbook §4.1). On `--complete`, prepare construction-replay assets (build-replay, naturalized narration, transcript PDF/TXT). Do **not** record `construction-replay.mp4` unless the user asks or clicks **Create construction video** on the Info tab (`--video` to opt in). **Narration must sound like a human demo** — follow `.cursor/rules/construction-narration-natural.mdc` before shipping transcript/video. Retain a short completion note in Hindsight bank `PilotFish-Sandbox`.
17. **Demo Docker inventory (required):** during/after builds (and when asked), run `python3 tools/list_sandbox_demo_docker.py` to report how many Sandbox Compose projects + `pf-*`/pilotfish containers are running. Record this demo’s compose project name and counts in `build-timing.json`. On **new demo start**, stop other Clients/ demos first (see `.cursor/rules/demo-docker-one-at-a-time.mdc`). Never prune or `down -v` without explicit user OK (playbook §5.1).
18. **SNIP HTML report (when demos write SNIP XML):** copy `snip_report.py` + `xslt/` from `edi-837-snip-sqlserver`. `/api/snip-report` must pass **EDI text strings** into `build_snip_html(snip_xml, edi_text)` — never a `Path`. HTML tab uses an iframe; fallback must show a short error, not raw/escaped SNIP XML (playbook §6.3).
19. **HTTP Post → queue (23R1):** do not re-debug the two slow loops from `http-post-to-rabbitmq`. RabbitMQ: **Host and Port** + `VirtualHost=/` (URI `amqp://host:5672/` yields empty vhost → 530). HTTP Post into a queue: **`Synchronous=false`** (`SyncAck` on the transport does not finish the HTTP wait). Opaque JSON: `NullRoutingModule`, not XPath. Copy `Clients/Demos/Other/http-post-to-rabbitmq/` (playbook §1.4).
20. **Promote timing speedups:** when `build-timing.json` `speedup_ideas` would skip a debug loop on the next demo, write them into the playbook §1.4 / §10 in the same session. The Timing tab is not enough.
21. **XML file as the outbound artifact:** put `com.pilotfish.eip.modules.transform.XMLFormattingProcessor` on the **transport** (Target processors) before `DirectoryTransport` / file write. Do not put it on the listener — that has no effect. Pretty-prints with 2-space indent. See playbook §1.4.
